.TH DEV_STACK 7 "2026-11-27" "dev_stack" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
dev_stack \- reference for the provisioned development environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B man 7 dev_stack
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual describes command-line tools, shell configuration, tmux behavior,
Neovim mappings, and configuration files deployed by the dev_stack Ansible
roles. Availability can depend on the target operating system and the role
tasks selected for a run.
.SH "TOOLS (CLI & runtimes)"
.TP
.B fzf
Fuzzy finder with Bash key bindings: Ctrl-R searches command history, Ctrl-T
selects files and previews them with
.BR bat ,
and Alt-C selects directories.
.TP
.B fd, fdfind
File finder; the role installs
.B fd
and provides
.B fdfind
as a compatibility symlink.
.TP
.B zoxide
Directory-jump tool; its Bash integration provides
.B z
and interactive
.BR zi .
.TP
.B bat, batcat
Command-line file viewer; the role provides
.B batcat
as a compatibility symlink.
.TP
.B ripgrep, rg
Text-search tool and its commonly used short command name.
.TP
.B yq
YAML command-line processor.
.TP
.B direnv
Per-directory environment loader, configured with a Bash hook. Use
.B direnv allow
to trust the current
.I .envrc
and
.B direnv deny
to revoke that approval.
.TP
.B uv, uvx
Python package and project tool, with its companion
.B uvx
executable.
.TP
.B try
The
.I binpash/try
utility is installed at
.BR /usr/local/bin/try .
.TP
.B lazygit
Terminal interface for Git.
.TP
.B starship
Shell prompt.
.TP
.B gh
GitHub command-line interface.
.TP
.B copilot
GitHub Copilot CLI.
.TP
.B agy
Google Antigravity CLI.
.TP
.B tmux
Terminal multiplexer (version 3.8); see
.B TMUX WORKFLOWS
below.
.TP
.B nvim
Neovim text editor (version 0.12.6); see
.B NEOVIM KEYMAPS & WORKFLOWS
below.
.TP
.B aws
AWS command-line interface.
.TP
.B docker
Docker Engine and command-line client; Docker Compose is installed as the
Compose plugin.
.TP
.B go
Go toolchain.
.TP
.B helm
Helm command-line tool.
.TP
.B oc
OpenShift command-line client.
.TP
.B C/C++ tools
The role installs GCC (
.BR gcc ,
.BR g++ ),
Clang (
.BR clang ),
CMake (
.BR cmake ),
and
.BR make
(with platform-appropriate packages).
.TP
.B pyenv, python3
Python version manager and Python runtimes. The configured versions are
3.13.2 (default), 3.12.9, and 3.11.11.
.TP
.B java, sdkman
Java 21 is installed using OpenJDK on Debian-family systems and Amazon
Corretto on Amazon Linux; SDKMAN! is also installed for Java SDK management.
.TP
.B nvm, node
Node Version Manager and Node.js; the configured Node.js version is 23.
.TP
.B tree-sitter
Tree-sitter command-line tool (version 0.22.6).
.TP
.B luacheck
Lua linter.
.TP
.B Basic utilities
The base role installs
.BR wget ,
.BR zip ,
.BR unzip ,
.BR tar ,
.BR git ,
.BR make ,
.BR jq ,
.BR bash-completion ,
.BR ca-certificates ,
.BR htop ,
.BR attr ,
and
.BR rsync .
.SH "SHELL ALIASES & FUNCTIONS"
The Bash aliases are defined in
.IR ~/.bash_aliases .
The following names and definitions are deployed:
.PP
.B "alias ddu=\fI'bash -c \(dq$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PrzemyslawSagalo/dev_stack/main/bootstrap.sh)\(dq'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gs=\fI'git status'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gcb=\fI'git branch --show-current'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gpcb=\fI'git push origin $(gcb)'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gacw=\fI'git commit -am wip'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gdcb=\fI'git pull origin $(gcb)'\fP"
.br
.B "alias gl=\fI'git log'\fP"
.br
.B "alias geb=\fI'export cb=$(gcb)'\fP"
.br
.B "alias lg=\fI'lazygit'\fP"
.br
.B "alias tnwc=\fI'tmux new-window -c $(pwd)'\fP"
.br
.B "alias pae=\fI'source venv/bin/activate'\fP"
.br
.B "alias pce=\fI'python -m venv venv && pae && pip install python-toolbox-przemek'\fP"
.br
.B "alias putb=\fI'pip install \(dqpython-toolbox-przemek[lint,tests]\(dq'\fP"
.br
.B "alias ptcr=\fI'coverage report -m'\fP"
.br
.B "alias se=\fI'set -a && source .env && set +a'\fP"
.br
.B "alias nv=\fI'nvim .'\fP"
.br
.B "alias cop=\fI'copilot'\fP"
.br
.B "alias agyyolo=\fI'agy --dangerously-skip-permissions'\fP"
.PP
.B gsquash
is a shell function with the signature
.BR "gsquash [commit-hash]" .
It collapses commits after the selected commit into that commit and preserves
its message, using a soft reset followed by an amend. Without an argument it
chooses the first commit ahead of the detected base branch. The working tree
must be clean; the function rejects a non-ancestor target and histories with
merge commits.
.PP
.B gacw
commits changes to tracked files only; it does not stage untracked files.
.B geb
exports the current branch name in the shell variable
.BR cb .
.B tnwc
opens a new tmux window rooted in the current directory.
.B se
sources
.I .env
with automatic exporting enabled while it is read.
.SH "TMUX WORKFLOWS"
The deployed
.I ~/.tmux.conf
sets the default terminal to
.BR tmux-256color ,
enables focus events and mouse mode, and advertises RGB true-color and
clipboard terminal features. Clipboard settings enable OSC 52 pass-through
to the outer terminal when that terminal supports it.
.PP
Copy mode uses vi keys. In copy mode,
.B y
copies the selection and exits; ending a mouse drag copies the selection
without clearing it. A mouse click selects the pane and clears the selection.
.PP
For two monitors, tmux's native grouped-session workflow can attach both
terminals to the same set of windows while retaining a separate current-window
selection per session. Start the first session with
.BR "tmux new-session -s work" .
On the other monitor, join that session group with
.BR "tmux new-session -t work" .
In general, use
.BR "tmux new-session -t <target>"
with the existing session as
.IR target .
This uses tmux's built-in session grouping; no dev_stack-specific helper is
installed for it.
.SH "NEOVIM KEYMAPS & WORKFLOWS"
The leader key is Space. The following core mappings come from the general
keymap configuration:
.TP
.B <leader>h, <leader>j, <leader>k, <leader>l
Move between windows left, down, up, and right.
.TP
.B <leader>y, <leader>p, <leader>P
In normal mode, yank to, paste from, or paste before from the system
clipboard. In visual mode,
.B <leader>y
and
.B <leader>p
yank to and paste from the system clipboard.
.TP
.B <leader><Up>, <leader><Down>, <leader><Left>, <leader><Right>
Resize the current window by two rows or columns in the indicated direction.
.TP
.B <S-l>, <S-h>
Move to the next or previous buffer.
.TP
.B <leader>q
Delete the current buffer with
.BR Bdelete .
.TP
.B kj
In insert mode, leave insert mode.
.TP
.B >, <
In visual mode, indent or unindent and keep the selection selected.
.TP
.B <A-j>, <A-k>
In visual mode, move the selected lines down or up.
.TP
.B p
In visual mode, paste without replacing the default register with the deleted
selection.
.TP
.B J, K, <A-j>, <A-k>
In visual-block mode, move the block down or up.
.TP
.B <C-h>, <C-j>, <C-k>, <C-l>
In terminal mode, leave terminal input and move to the neighboring window.
.B <Esc>
and
.B kj
also leave terminal input.
.TP
.B :DiffOrig
Show a vertical diff between the current buffer and the original file on disk.
.PP
Plugin mappings:
.TP
.B <leader>ff
Telescope: find files in the current working directory.
.TP
.B <leader>fa
Telescope: find files including ignored and hidden files.
.TP
.B <leader>fg
Telescope: search project text with live grep.
.TP
.B <leader>e
Toggle the nvim-tree explorer. In its buffer,
.B l, <CR>, o
opens a node,
.B h
closes a node, and
.B v
opens a file in a vertical split.
.TP
.B <leader>a
Toggle Aerial's symbol outline; within an attached buffer,
.B {
and
.B }
move to the previous and next symbol.
.TP
.B <leader>tc, <leader>tf, <leader>ta
Neotest: run the nearest test, the current file's tests, or all test files.
.TP
.B <leader>td, <leader>ts, <leader>tm
Neotest: debug the nearest test, stop a run, or toggle the summary and output
panel.
.TP
.B <leader>gl, <leader>ca
LSP: show diagnostic details in a float, or invoke a code action.
.TP
.B <leader>cc
Toggle a comment on the current line in normal mode or the selection in
visual mode.
.TP
.B s, S, gs
Leap: jump forward, jump backward, or jump from another window.
.TP
.B <leader>dc, <leader>do, <leader>di, <leader>du
DAP: continue, step over, step into, or step out.
.TP
.B <leader>db, <leader>dk, <leader>dt, <leader>dr
DAP: toggle a breakpoint, set a conditional breakpoint, terminate, or clear
breakpoints.
.TP
.B <leader>dm, <leader>df, <leader>dx
DAP: toggle the UI, open a floating UI element, or debug the current Python
test method.
.TP
.B <M-\e>, <M-]>, <M-[>, <M-w>
Copilot: accept a suggestion, select the next or previous suggestion, or
dismiss it, respectively.
.PP
Core options disable GUI cursor-shape changes and error bells, enable absolute
and relative line numbers, four-space
indentation with spaces, smart indent, incremental search without persistent
search highlighting, no line wrapping or swap file, persistent undo, a
sign column, and terminal true color. Automatic file reload is enabled with
a 200 ms update time. The system clipboard uses OSC 52; over SSH or tmux,
paste uses the cached copied text.
.SH "CONFIGURATION FILES"
The dotfiles role deploys or manages the following paths:
.TP
.I ~/.tmux.conf
Tmux terminal, color, clipboard, mouse, focus, and copy-mode settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/nvim
Neovim configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.bash_aliases
Shell aliases and the
.B gsquash
function; sourced from
.IR ~/.bashrc .
.TP
.I ~/.config/starship.toml
Starship prompt configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ai/
Shared AI CLI configuration, including skills, standards, agents, commands,
and shared configuration files. Its entries are symlinked into the
corresponding client locations under
.IR ~/.copilot/ ,
.IR ~/.gemini/config/ ,
and
.IR ~/.config/opencode/ .
.TP
.I ~/.config/bash/init.sh
Bash initialization sourced from
.IR ~/.bashrc .
.TP
.I ~/.bashrc
Interactive Bash configuration and sourcing entries.
.TP
.I ~/.gitconfig
Deployed Git configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.gitconfig.local
Optional local Git user identity configuration, initialized when missing.
.TP
.I ~/.gitignore_global
Global Git ignore file.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
SSH configuration with a dotfiles-managed block.
.TP
.I ~/.gemini/config/
Google Antigravity configuration and shared AI symlinks.
.TP
.I ~/.copilot/
GitHub Copilot configuration and shared AI symlinks.
.TP
.I ~/.config/opencode/
OpenCode configuration and shared AI symlinks.
